## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of a beginner-friendly CQRS/event-sourcing workflow with cross-service coordination, compensation patterns, and concrete read model projections.

## Key Concepts

- Append-only EventStore per aggregate root
- Simple saga orchestration with compensation logic
- Read model projection from event streams
- Event-driven communication between bounded contexts

## Code Example

```javascript
// Data contracts
class OrderPlaced { constructor(orderId, items, amount) { this.orderId = orderId; this.items = items; this.amount = amount; } }
class InventoryReserved { constructor(orderId) { this.orderId = orderId; } }
class PaymentAuthorized { constructor(orderId) { this.orderId = orderId; } }
class PaymentFailed { constructor(orderId, reason) { this.orderId = orderId; this.reason = reason; } }
class InventoryRejected { constructor(orderId, reason) { this.orderId = orderId; this.reason = reason; } }

// Append-only EventStore per order
class EventStore {
  constructor() { this.events = new Map(); }
  append(orderId, event) {
    if (!this.events.has(orderId)) this.events.set(orderId, []);
    this.events.get(orderId).push(event);
  }
  getEvents(orderId) { return this.events.get(orderId) || []; }
}

// Saga Orchestrator
class OrderSaga {
  constructor(eventStore, inventoryService, paymentService) {
    this.eventStore = eventStore;
    this.inventory = inventoryService;
    this.payment = paymentService;
  }
  async handle(event) {
    if (event instanceof OrderPlaced) {
      this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, event);
      const inventoryResult = await this.inventory.reserve(event.orderId, event.items);
      if (inventoryResult.success) {
        this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, new InventoryReserved(event.orderId));
        const paymentResult = await this.payment.authorize(event.orderId, event.amount);
        if (paymentResult.success) {
          this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, new PaymentAuthorized(event.orderId));
        } else {
          this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, new PaymentFailed(event.orderId, paymentResult.reason));
          this.compensate(event.orderId);
        }
      } else {
        this.eventStore.append(event.orderId, new InventoryRejected(event.orderId, inventoryResult.reason));
      }
    }
  }
  compensate(orderId) {
    const events = this.eventStore.getEvents(orderId);
    events.reverse().forEach(event => {
      if (event instanceof InventoryReserved) {
        this.inventory.release(orderId);
      }
    });
  }
}

// Read Model Projection
class OrderStatusProjection {
  constructor(eventStore) {
    this.eventStore = eventStore;
    this.orderStatus = new Map();
  }
  project(orderId) {
    const events = this.eventStore.getEvents(orderId);
    let status = 'Pending';
    events.forEach(event => {
      if (event instanceof PaymentAuthorized) status = 'Completed';
      else if (event instanceof PaymentFailed || event instanceof InventoryRejected) status = 'Failed';
    });
    this.orderStatus.set(orderId, status);
    return status;
  }
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design distributed workflow using sagas, CQRS, and event-sourcing in real-world microservices; probes handling of failure modes, idempotency, compensations, and consistency guarantees.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration vs choreography
- Event store and projections for CQRS
- Compensating actions and timeouts
- Idempotent handlers and outbox pattern

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: saga orchestrator pattern
class CheckoutSaga {
  async start(order) {
    await dispatch('ReserveInventory', order);
  }
  async onEvent(event) {
    if (event.type === 'InventoryReserved') await dispatch('CapturePayment', event.order);
    else if (event.type === 'PaymentCaptured') await dispatch('ScheduleShipment', event.order);
    else if (event.type === 'ShipmentScheduled') complete(event.order);
    else if (event.type.endsWith('Failed')) compensate(event.order);
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- What are the trade-offs between orchestration and choreography in this scenario?
- How would you test the saga under partial failures and timeouts?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design cross-region sagas with per-tenant isolation, durable storage, and reliable cleanup.

## Key Concepts
- Saga orchestration across regions with CQRS and Event Sourcing
- Per-tenant event envelopes and outbox pattern
- Compensating actions and idempotent handlers
- Replay-safe projections and cross-region read-model updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal orchestrator sketch (pseudo)
function startSaga(tenantId, mediaId){
  const sagaId = uuid();
  persistSaga({id:sagaId, tenantId, mediaId, step:'Transcode', status:'in_progress'});
  publish({type:'Ingest', payload:{tenantId, mediaId, sagaId}});
}
function handleFailure(sagaId, failedStep){
  const comp = {Transcode:'DeleteTempArtifacts', PublishEU:'RevokePublishEU'}[failedStep];
  publish({type:'Compensate', payload:{sagaId, action:comp}});
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you ensure idempotency across services during retries?
- How would you observe and reconcile outbox vs. internal state across regions?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests practical multi-tenant cache coherence across regions, combining Redis Pub/Sub and Memcached. It probes data structures, invalidation flow, and how to reason about latency and correctness in real systems.

## Key Concepts

- Tenant-scoped keys and version stamps
- Invalidation via Pub/Sub channels vs TTL-based expiry
- Cross-region consistency with Redis replication and a purge path for Memcached
- Bulk invalidations, race conditions, and stale reads

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal invalidation path
function onDataWrite(tenantId, key, newVer) {
  // publish invalidation
  cachePubSub.publish('inval:tenant:' + tenantId, { key, ver: newVer });
}
subscribe('inval:tenant:' + tenantId, msg => evictCacheIfOutdated(tenantId, msg.key, msg.ver));
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to coalesce bursts of invalidations for hot keys?
- How to measure and guarantee acceptable stale-read bounds?
